chat service, specifying 'fee waiver' in your query. The team will review your request and provide an update via push notification within 3 working days.\\n- If you miss a payment on multiple Horizon Bank credit cards, a consolidated statement is provided for all your cards, and you will be charged a single late fee applied across all your cards rather than separate fees for each individual card.\\n- Horizon Bank does not levy any issuance or annual fees for an additional supplementary card. All expenses incurred on the supplementary card are combined with the primary card’s balance, and any late-payment penalties or interest charges are applied exclusively to the main cardholder.\"}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"yes, and also what about the rate and the fee\"}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"Could you clarify what you mean by \\\"the rate and the fee\\\"? Are you asking about a personal loan or a credit card?\"}]\n\n    Natively generate response in: English\n\n    Rules:\n    - Only identify a topic as unresolved if the transcript clearly shows\n      one: a question the assistant never actually answered, a clarification\n      the assistant asked for that the customer never gave, or an escalation\n      that never concluded. A session that ended with a complete answer, or\n      that was only ever a greeting with nothing else in it, has nothing\n      unresolved -- do not invent a topic to follow up on.\n    - If a topic is unresolved, name it in your own words (never quote\n      internal ids) and ask, in one sentence, whether the customer would\n      like to continue it.\n    - Do not repeat or restate the login greeting itself.\n    - If there is no unresolved topic, or the transcript is empty, return an\n      empty string -- an empty follow-up is the normal, expected outcome for\n      most logins, not a failure.\n    - Keep it to at most two sentences. Do not invent any fact, banking\n      procedure, or policy not present above.\n\n    Ou