redit limit.\\n- **For new applicants:**\\n  * Singapore citizens, permanent residents, and foreign nationals are all permitted to apply for the Instant Loan.\\n  * Every submission will be subject to Horizon Bank’s credit‑worthiness assessment.\\n\\nYou may request a credit facility provided you satisfy the following criteria:\\n- You are aged between {{faq_0ae0bb51_001}} and {{faq_0ae0bb51_002}} years.\\n- Your annual income is at least {{faq_0ae0bb51_003}} if you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\\n- Your annual income is at least {{faq_0ae0bb51_004}} if you are a foreigner holding a valid work pass.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"resolved_request\": \"credit card fees and charges\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_1b3f3507\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank's foreign transaction fee policy work for international purchases made with my Horizon card?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we do not impose any foreign transaction or markup fees on your Horizon card, including the standard {{faq_1b3f3507_001}} fee typically charged by Visa. However, please note that when you use your Horizon card for international transactions through third-party payment platforms like Alipay or WeChat Pay, these platforms may charge their own service fees for processing international card payments. For details on any applicable fees, we recommend checking directly with the relevant payment platform.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_2ba8c382\", \"content\": \"Question: If I fail to make a payment on multiple Horizon Bank credit cards, will I incur a late fee for each card or a single fee for my combined statement?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we provide a consolidated statement for all your Horizon cards. In the event of a missed payment, you will be charged a single late fee, which will be applied across all your Horizon cards, rather than incurring separate late fees for each individual card.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_4659512d\", \"content\": \"Questio