{"timestamp": "2026-08-29T05:52:27.596+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_2a64d2b1-d6cf-44bd-ace2-8a260af0fed1", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): what's the required docs?\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nAI: Welcome back, Benson! How can I help with your banking today? Also, you still have 6 pending requests (Change Address and Resubmit KYC Document) — you can check them anytime from the requests icon in the top right.\n\nWould you like to continue discussing the account or service fees you asked about earlier, or apply for a card?\nUser: what's the required docs?\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Submit identification documents through the secure portal or visit a branch for verification.\", \"policy\": \"Valid government-issued identification and proof of address are mandatory for all account holders.\", \"conceptual\": \"Know Your Customer (KYC) is a mandatory regulatory process to verify identity and prevent fraud.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"ALL\", \"target_intent\": [\"General Inquiries\"], \"customer_component\": \"What are the required documents for the KYC resubmission process?\", \"direct_query\": \"What are the required documents for the KYC resubmission process?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Submit identification documents through the secure portal or visit a branch for verification.\", \"policy\": \"Valid government-issued identification and proof of address are mandatory for all account holders.\", \"conceptual\": \"Know Your Customer (KYC) is a mandatory regulatory process to verify identity and prevent fraud.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_ed92e41d\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps can I take to confirm that an email claiming to be from Horizon Bank is authentic?\\n\\nAnswer: - Horizon Bank will only send messages from an address that finishes with @horizonbank.sg.  \\n- We will never request your password, PIN, or any confidential account details via email.  \\n- If you are unsure about a message, reach out to our Customer Care team at +{{faq_ed92e41d_001}} {{faq_ed92e41d_002}}- HORIZ ( +{{faq_ed92e41d_003}} {{faq_ed92e41d_004}} {{faq_ed92e41d_005}} ) or connect with us through the in‑app chat or a phone call.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_ded247c0\", \"content\": \"Question: What sets Horizon Bank apart from traditional banking institutions?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we've revolutionized the banking experience by leveraging cutting-edge technology to create a seamless, mobile-first platform. By streamlining processes and eliminating the need for physical branches, we're able to provide our customers with a {{faq_ded247c0_001}}/{{faq_ded247c0_002}} banking service that's both convenient and efficient. A prime illustration of this is our expedited sign-up process, which can be completed in mere minutes for Singapore residents utilizing Singpass, highlighting our commitment to simplicity and speed.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_7fc44444\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank collaborate with regulatory bodies to combat cyber threats and protect customers from fraudulent activities?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we are committed to safeguarding our customers' interests through a collaborative approach with the Monetary Authority of Singapore and other relevant authorities. The Shared Responsibility Framework is a pivotal initiative that underscores the importance of joint efforts between banks, regulatory bodies, and customers in preventing and mitigating the impact of scams. This framework specifically addresses vulnerabilities that scammers may exploit, including impersonation of legitimate entities, such as government agencies or financial institutions like Horizon Bank, where fraudsters deceive customers into divulging sensitive information. Additionally, it tackles the risks associated with malicious links sent via digital platforms, which can lead to the compromise of account credentials. By promoting a culture of shared responsibility, we aim to empower our customers with the knowledge and best practices necessary to secure their financial information and transactions, thereby fostering a safer digital banking environment for all.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_a171e351\", \"content\": \"Question: Can you tell me about the background of Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: Horizon Bank, operating under the Horizon brand, is a pioneering digital banking institution, born out of an innovative collaboration between a prominent international banking group and a local social enterprise. This distinctive alliance leverages the strengths of both partners, combining over two centuries of collective experience serving the Singapore market.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents. `customer_component` may already be elaborated with\n          retrieval-oriented wording the customer never actually said, so\n          if you set `unresolved_term` below, derive it by reasoning\n          directly against Original User Message and Trusted Conversation\n          Context instead -- never by quoting `customer_component` back --\n          a clarifying question must quote something the customer will\n          recognize as their own.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially pr