k in conjunction with the PayNow scheme operator to ensure that your PayNow name reflects your registered account name on record. This collaborative effort guarantees that rigorous checks are in place to verify the correctness of your updated PayNow name, providing you with assurance of its accuracy.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_9470585b\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank protect my identity when I send payments, and what information is shared with the recipient?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we prioritize your privacy and security. When you receive payments through the Horizon App, your partial name is displayed to help prevent impersonation scams. However, as a sender, your full name will appear on the recipient's statement and transaction records. This standard practice across major payment schemes supports various business use cases, such as validating investment funds or resolving disputes. It also helps identify potential scams or fraud by allowing recipients to verify the source of funds. This measure is in place to ensure the integrity of transactions and provide an additional layer of security for our customers.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_5b37494f\", \"content\": \"Question: What should I prepare and bring when I visit a Horizon Bank Experience Centre?\\n\\nAnswer: - If you filed a paper application before {{faq_5b37494f_001}} Dec {{faq_5b37494f_002}} and did not use MyInfo, you must appear at a Horizon Bank Experience Centre for in‑person identity verification. Bring the original identification documents:\\n  • NRIC for Singapore citizens or permanent residents.\\n  • Passport for Work Pass or Dependent Pass holders.\\n- A Horizon representative will confirm your identity and continue processing your request.\\n- You can monitor the application’s progress through the Horizon App.\\n- From {{faq_5b37494f_003}} Dec {{faq_5b37494f_004}} onward, we advise using MyInfo authentication for a faster, more secure submission. Ensure your SingPass details 