{"timestamp": "2026-08-29T07:14:53.337+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_1f1176c3-1e12-4d8b-8636-a65c85448b9e", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): I am asking about interest rates for a personal loan.\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nAI: Welcome back, Benson! How can I help with your banking today? Also, you still have 8 pending requests (Resubmit KYC Document and Change Address) — you can check them anytime from the requests icon in the top right.\n\nWould you like to continue discussing the required documents for your KYC resubmission?\nUser: doc'\nAI: I currently do not have any information available regarding the documents required for the KYC (Know Your Customer, a verification process used to confirm your identity) resubmission process. 📄\nUser: what's the fee\nAI: 📋 I currently do not have the details available regarding the fees associated with the KYC (Know Your Customer, a verification process used to confirm your identity) resubmission process.\nUser: i am not talking aobut kyc\nAI: Understood, how else can I assist you today? 😊\nUser: tell me the rate\nAI: Could you please clarify what you mean by \"the current interest rate\"? Specifically, are you asking about a deposit account, a personal loan, or a credit card? 💳\nUser: i want the rate, the fee, the account\nAI: 🔍 Could you please clarify what you mean by \"interest rates for a bank account\"? Let us know if you are referring to a deposit account, a personal loan, or a credit card.\n\n💳 Could you also clarify what you mean by \"fees associated with a bank account\"? Please specify if this is for a deposit account, a credit card, or a personal loan.\n\n📂 Additionally, could you clarify what you mean by \"bank account details or types\"? Specifically, let us know if you are asking about deposit account types.\nUser: I am asking about interest rates for a personal loan.\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Reviewing the current interest rate calculation methods and payout schedules for personal loan accounts.\", \"policy\": \"Understanding the eligibility criteria and bonus interest rate conditions applicable to personal loan products.\", \"conceptual\": \"Defining how interest rates are applied to personal loan balances and the impact of repayment terms.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Personal_Loan\", \"target_intent\": [\"Account Management\", \"Application\", \"Authentication And Security\", \"Eligibility\", \"Features And Limits\", \"Fees And Charges\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Interest And Rates\", \"Loan And Credit Management\", \"Rewards And Promotions\"], \"customer_component\": \"What are the current interest rates for a personal loan?\", \"direct_query\": \"What are the current interest rates for a personal loan?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Reviewing the current interest rate calculation methods and payout schedules for personal loan accounts.\", \"policy\": \"Understanding the eligibility criteria and bonus interest rate conditions applicable to personal loan products.\", \"conceptual\": \"Defining how interest rates are applied to personal loan balances and the impact of repayment terms.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The supplied parents discuss the Effective Interest Rate calculation for borrowing costs generally and credit card interest rates specifically, but neither provides information regarding interest rates for personal loans.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_75ed6e4d\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the typical timeframe for my loan to be approved?\\n\\nAnswer: - The vast majority of loans are approved and the amount is deposited into your Horizon savings account in about {{faq_75ed6e4d_001}} seconds.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_9b1617de\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank define the Effective Interest Rate (EIR) for its loans?\\n\\nAnswer: - The Effective Interest Rate (EIR) indicates the genuine cost of borrowing from Horizon Bank. It incorporates the decreasing principal balance over the life of the loan together with all applicable charges, including the annual fee applied in the first year.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_2109a75e\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank calculate the monthly payment for my loan?\\n\\nAnswer: - The monthly payment is computed by summing the approved principal amount with the total interest that will accrue over the loan term, and then dividing that combined figure by the total number of months in the loan period. For additional details, please consult the Horizon Instant Loan Terms & Conditions.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_8984208c\", \"content\": \"Question: What charges does Horizon Bank apply to an Instant Loan?\\n\\nAnswer: - No annual fee is levied on Instant Loans that were originated before {{faq_8984208c_001}} February {{faq_8984208c_002}}.\\n- For Instant Loans opened on or after {{faq_8984208c_003}} February {{faq_8984208c_004}}:\\n  * A first‑year annual charge equal to {{faq_8984208c_005}} % of the loan amount is added to your Horizon credit card.\\n  * If the loan term is one year or longer, a {{faq_8984208c_006}} anniversary fee is assessed each year the loan remains outstanding, but only when the minimum payment on your Horizon credit card has not been received by its due date for the preceding {{faq_8984208c_007}} consecutive calendar months.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents. `customer_component` may already be elaborated with\n          retrieval-oriented wording the customer never actually said, so\n          if you set `unresolved_term` below, derive it by reasoning\n          directly against Original User Message and Trusted Conversation\n          Context instead -- never by quoting `customer_component` back --\n          a clarifying question must quote something the customer will\n          recognize as their own.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly