mes a shortcut not present in\n          \"available_shortcuts\", invents a detail beyond the supplied\n          label/topic/for_request (a step, field, screen layout, url, count,\n          or id), claims a shortcut replaces or invalidates a *different*\n          evidence-based answer than the one its own for_request names, or\n          claims execution/completion. Do not reject a compliant statement\n          merely for existing, and do not require decline/apology framing\n          for a subquery whose only coverage is a matching shortcut.\n        - \"unavailable_service_requests\" entries are a permitted source only\n          for a brief sentence stating that part of the request could not be\n          started, using only the supplied reason. Any different explanation\n          is unsupported.\n        - \"verified_api_context\" entries are a permitted factual source, on\n          the same footing as Task-Level Approved Evidence, but each entry\n          supports only the exact statement in its own `fact` text -- no\n          extrapolation beyond it.\n        - \"personal_data_placeholders\" entries permit a customer-facing\n          sentence to include an entry's `insert_token` verbatim when the\n          sentence addresses that same entry's `for_request`. The sentence\n          must never state, paraphrase, or guess the real value the token\n          represents (it is never disclosed to the assistant, so it can\n          never legitimately appear as prose) and must never use a\n          `{data-*}` token that is not present in this list.\n        \n\n        ============================================================\n        Customer-Facing Content (assess against BOTH axes above):\n        \n        Original Customer Message (courtesy-context only; never a source for a\n        banking fact, instruction, product capability, policy, or outcome):\n        \"just that\"\n\n        Optional Internal Response-Element Provenance (not customer-facing):\n        []\n\n        Clarification Inputs (the only source for what a clarifying\n        question may be about -- exactly what the generator itself was\n        given, nothing more: \"scope\" names where in the pipeline the\n        ambiguity blocks progress, \"unresolved_request\" is the specific\n        thing that's unclear -- the generator composed its own question\n        from this, there is no fixed sentence to compare against -- and\n        0-3 \"clarification_guesses\" are PREDICTIONS of likely customer\n        intent, never reports of anything actually said):\n        [{\"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"scope\": \"Classifying whether this request is a compliant banking question, an explicit request for a human agent, or something outside what this assistant can help with, before any decomposition into components was attempted.\", \"unresolved_request\": \"whether the user wants to resubmit their KYC document or change their address\", \"clarification_guesses\": [{\"label\": \"Resubmit KYC\", \"message\": \"I would like to resubmit my KYC document.\", \"reason\": \"The user has a pending request for KYC document resubmission.\"}, {\"label\": \"Change Address\", \"message\": \"I would like to change my address.\", \"reason\": \"The user has a pending request for address change.\"}]}]\n\n        Terminal Unresolved Task Markers (topic/status only; never evidence):\n        []\n\n        Decline Inputs (the only source for a declined-topic explanation):\n        []\n\n        No-Info Inputs (the only source for an unavailable-information statement):\n        []\n\n        Customer-Facing Answer:\n        \"\"\n\n        Customer-Facing Clarification:\n        \"Please let me know if you would like to proceed with resubmitting your KYC document (meaning your Know Your Customer identity verification documents) or if you would like to change your address 📋.\"\n\n        Complete Customer-Facing UI Payload:\n        \"{\"uiType\": \"blocks\", \"options\": [], \"stepDetails\": [], \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"items\": [], \"extendedText\": \"\", \"listClarificationText\": \"\", \"responseBlocks\": [{\"type\": \"clarification\", \"text\": \"Please let me know if you would like to proceed with resubmitting your KYC document (meaning your Know Your Customer identity verification documents) or if you would like to change your address 📋.\", \"options\": [{\"label\": \"Resubmit KYC\", \"message\": \"I would like to resubmit my KYC document.\"}, {\"label\": \"Change Address\", \"message\": \"I would like to change my address.\"}]}]}\"\n        \n\n        Output JSON only:\n        {\"conduct_compliant\": true/false, \"conduct_reason\": \"...\", \"conduct_violations\": [{\"rule\": \"bank_conduct\" | \"regulation\", \"violation\": \"...\", \"unsupported_content\": [\"verbatim phrase\"]}], \"answer_compliant\": true/false, \"clarification_compliant\": true/false, \"rewrite_instruction\": \"...\", \"evidence_grounded\": true/false, \"evidence_reason\": \"...\", \"evidence_violations\": [{\"scope\": \"...\", \"unsupported_content\": [\"verbatim phrase\"], \"evidence_gap\": \"...\"}], \"answer_evidence_grounded\": true/false, \"answer_bridge_grounded\": true/false, \"clarification_grounded\": true/false, \"clarification_connected\": true/false, \"response_recovery_strategy\":\"NO_STRATEGY\" | \"REMOVE_UNSUPPORTED_CONTENT\" | \"NARROW_TO_EVIDENCE_SCOPE\" | \"CLARIFY_FROM_ALLOWED_CONTEXT\", \"grounding_violations\": [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"scope\": \"answer\" | \"ui_payload\" | \"clarification\", \"audit_layer\": \"evidence\" | \"bridge\" | \"other\", \"violation_type\": \"unsupported_factual_claim\" | \"unsupported_bridge_inference\" | \"unsupported_instruction\" | \"wrong_task_evidence\" | \"unsupported_clarification_suggestion\" | \"missing_decline_reference\" | \"task_not_answered\" | \"other\", \"unsupported_content\": [\"verbatim customer-facing phrase\"], \"evidence_gap\": \"missing permitted evidence o