ur application form. If you delete or reinstall the Horizon App after successfully registering, you will still need to authenticate via SingPass when you log in again.\n\nTo apply for a credit card, Singaporean citizens and permanent residents can use MyInfo for expedited form completion on the secure Horizon Bank web portal, which can be initiated through a partner's mobile app or website. Foreign applicants should ensure they have their passport and most recent payslip ready for upload or photo capture via the Horizon App, in addition to accessing MyInfo. You will receive immediate status updates and prompts for any additional actions required within the app.\n\nIf you already possess a Horizon credit card and have an adequate unused credit limit, you may apply for Horizon Bank's Instant Loan offering, provided you meet the general eligibility criteria such as age limits and annual income requirements. Every submission is subject to Horizon Bank's credit-worthiness assessment.\nUser: what docs\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Complete the application form using MyInfo verification for automated data population.\", \"policy\": \"Applicants must provide valid identification documents as specified by bank security protocols.\", \"conceptual\": \"A savings account is a deposit product designed for individual financial management and growth.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Deposit_Account\", \"target_intent\": [\"Application\"], \"customer_component\": \"What documents are required to open a savings account at Horizon Bank?\", \"direct_query\": \"What documents are required to open a savings account at Horizon Bank?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Complete the application form using MyInfo verification for automated data population.\", \"policy\": \"Applicants must provide valid identification documents as specified by bank security protocols.\", \"conceptual\": \"A savings account is a deposit product designed for individual financial management and growth.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_70aebcd6\", \"content\": \"Question: What information and tools are necessary to open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - A mobile phone together with MyInfo verification to auto‑populate your application form.\\n- If you delete or reinstall the Horizon App after successfully registering, you will still need to authenticate via SingPass when you log in again.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"procedural\": \"Upload required identification and income proof documents through the secure bank portal.\", \"policy\": \"Applicants must meet age and income requirements and provide necessary verification documentation.\", \"conceptual\": \"A credit card provides a revolving line of credit for individual consumer purchases.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Credit_Card\", \"target_intent\": [\"Application\"], \"customer_component\": \"What documents are required to apply for a Horizon Bank credit card?\", \"direct_query\": \"What documents are required to apply for a Horizon Bank credit card?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_2\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Upload required identification and income proof documents through the secure bank portal.\", \"policy\": \"Applicants must meet age and income requirements and provide necessary verification documentation.\", \"conceptual\": \"A credit card provides a revolving line of credit for individual consumer purchases.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_85dbaadf\", \"content\": \"Question: What documentation is required to initiate a Horizon Bank credit card application?\\n\\nAnswer: To streamline your credit card application with Horizon Bank, Singaporean citizens and permanent residents can utilize MyInfo for expedited form completion. For foreign applicants, please ensure you have your passport and most recent payslip readily available for upload or photo capture via the Horizon App, in addition to accessing MyInfo.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_dea282b8\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for using Horizon Bank’s online credit‑card application?\\n\\nAnswer: - Initiate a Horizon credit‑card request through a partner’s mobile app or website.\\n- The submission is handled on a secure Horizon Bank web portal.\\n- Utilize the MyInfo service to auto‑populate your personal details.\\n- Receive immediate status updates, and be prompted for any additional actions required within the Horizon App.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_c241b12d\", \"content\": \"Question: As a senior citizen, am I eligible to apply for a Horizon Bank credit card, and what are the key requirements I need to fulfill?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we welcome applications from retirees who meet specific criteria. To qualify for our credit card with a credit limit of {{faq_c241b12d_001}}, you must be a Singapore citizen or permanent resident, aged {{faq_c241b12d_002}} or above, have an assessed annual income of less than {{faq_c241b12d_003}}, and not hold any existing credit cards or unsecured loans with us. If you meet these conditions, you may be eligible for our credit card, subject to our standard banking requirements.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_d5c931d4\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps do I need to take to enroll in Horizon Bank's Visa Instalment program for my purchases?\\n\\nAnswer: To apply for Horizon Bank's Visa Instalment program, follow these steps: \\n   - When shopping online with participating merchants, identify the 'Instalments enabled by Visa' logo at checkout. Enter your Horizon card details, and available instalment plans will be presented. Choose your preferred plan and finalize your payment.\\n   - For in-store purchases, after tapping your card to pay, you will be shown the available instalment plans. Select the one that suits you best and complete the transaction. \\n   Upon successful enrolment, you will receive a notification through the Horizon App. Please note that the minimum transaction amount to qualify for this program is {{faq_d5c931d4_001}}. Only primary Horizon credit cards are eligible, and if you have a linked card, ensure it is paired with your main credit card account. Debit cards and supplementary credit cards are not eligible for instalment plans and will be charged the full amount upfront.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"procedural\": \"Submit loan application via the mobile app after verifying existing credit limit availability.\", \"policy\": \"Loan approval is subject to credit-worthiness assessment and meeting minimum income criteria.\", \"conceptual\": \"An instant loan is a personal credit facility offering quick access to funds.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Personal_Loan\", \"target_intent\": [\"Application\"], \"customer_component\": \"What documents are required to apply for a Horizon Bank instant loan?\", \"direct_query\": \"What documents are required to apply for a Horizon Bank instant loan?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_3\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Submit loan application via the mobile app after verifying existing credit limit availability.\", \"policy\": \"Loan approval is subject to credit-worthiness assessment and meeting minimum income criteria.\", \"conceptual\": \"An instant loan is a personal credit facility offering quick access to funds.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_f9cce3c1\", \"content\": \"Question: If my Instant Loan request is declined, can I still submit applications for other Horizon Bank products such as a credit card or a savings account?\\n\\nAnswer: - Absolutely. A declined loan does not prevent you from applying for other Horizon Bank offerings. You simply need to start a new application tailored to the specific product you wish to obtain.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_46c17d0e\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps do I need to take to initiate a balance transfer request with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To begin the balance transfer process, navigate to the Horizon App, select the 'More' option, and then proceed to the 'Loan' section, where you will find 'Other Flexible Loans' to commence your application.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_75ed6e4d\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the typical timeframe for my loan to be approved?\\n\\nAnswer: - The vast majority of loans are approved and the amount is deposited into your Horizon savings account in about {{faq_75ed6e4d_001}} seconds.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents. `customer_component` may already be elaborated with\n          retrieval-oriented wording the customer never actually said, so\n          if you set `unresolved_term` below, derive it by reasoning\n          directly against Original User Message and Trusted Conversation\n          Context instead -- never by quoting `customer_component` back --\n          a clarifying question must quote something the customer will\n          recognize as their own.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - The reverse matters just as much: a parent whose own subject is a\n          distinctly-named, different product or service is not material\n          merely because it is credit/loan-adjacent, belongs to the same\n          broader family, or is reached through the same in-app menu path as\n          the customer's named product. For example, a balance transfer\n          draws on loan credit and is filed under the app's \"Loan\" section\n          alongside a personal loan application -- but a parent describing\n          how to request a balance transfer does not materially answer a\n          request about applying for a (personal/general) loan. Do not let\n          shared category vocabulary or menu wording (\"Loan section\",\n          \"commence your application\") substitute for the parent actually\n          being about the specific product or process the customer named.\n          Only treat a differently-named product's parent as material when\n          it explicitly states it also applies to, or is the general form\n          of, the customer's named product.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,