{"timestamp": "2026-08-29T16:31:21.843+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_3e2f4119-8afe-4348-b435-558a24387f34", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): what docs\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nUser: what else\nAI: I am here to help you with your Horizon Bank questions. 😊\nUser: what else\nAI: I am always here to assist you with your Horizon Bank questions. 😊\nUser: i want that\nAI: Could you please let me know a bit more about what you are looking for, such as whether you would like to learn more about the general services Horizon Bank offers or if you are interested in opening a new savings account? 🤔\nUser: the other one\nAI: Could you please clarify if you would like to learn more about the general services Horizon Bank offers or if you are interested in opening a new savings account? 🤔\nUser: I would like to learn more about the general services Horizon Bank offers.\nAI: I do not currently have information available regarding the general banking services offered by Horizon Bank. 🏦\nUser: how to open an account and how to apply credit card and can i also apply for loan if i have credit card\nAI: To open a savings account with Horizon Bank, you will need a mobile phone along with MyInfo verification to auto-populate your application form. If you delete or reinstall the Horizon App after successfully registering, you will still need to authenticate via SingPass when you log in again.\n\nTo apply for a credit card, Singaporean citizens and permanent residents can use MyInfo for expedited form completion on the secure Horizon Bank web portal, which can be initiated through a partner's mobile app or website. Foreign applicants should ensure they have their passport and most recent payslip ready for upload or photo capture via the Horizon App, in addition to accessing MyInfo. You will receive immediate status updates and prompts for any additional actions required within the app.\n\nIf you already possess a Horizon credit card and have an adequate unused credit limit, you may apply for Horizon Bank's Instant Loan offering, provided you meet the general eligibility criteria such as age limits and annual income requirements. Every submission is subject to Horizon Bank's credit-worthiness assessment.\nUser: what docs\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"procedural\": \"Submit loan application via the mobile app after verifying existing credit limit availability.\", \"policy\": \"Loan approval is subject to credit-worthiness assessment and meeting minimum income criteria.\", \"conceptual\": \"An instant loan is a personal credit facility offering quick access to funds.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Personal_Loan\", \"target_intent\": [\"Account Management\", \"Application\", \"Authentication And Security\", \"Eligibility\", \"Features And Limits\", \"Fees And Charges\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Interest And Rates\", \"Loan And Credit Management\", \"Rewards And Promotions\"], \"customer_component\": \"What documents are required to apply for a Horizon Bank instant loan?\", \"direct_query\": \"What documents are required to apply for a Horizon Bank instant loan?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_3\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Submit loan application via the mobile app after verifying existing credit limit availability.\", \"policy\": \"Loan approval is subject to credit-worthiness assessment and meeting minimum income criteria.\", \"conceptual\": \"An instant loan is a personal credit facility offering quick access to funds.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"None of the provided parents contain information regarding the documentation required to apply for an Instant Loan. The parents discuss loan application procedures, balance transfers, and approval timeframes, but not the specific documents needed.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_0ae0bb51\", \"content\": \"Question: Do I qualify for Horizon Bank’s Instant Loan offering?\\n\\nAnswer: - **For current Horizon Bank clients:**\\n  * You need to possess a Horizon credit card and have adequate unused credit limit.\\n- **For new applicants:**\\n  * Singapore citizens, permanent residents, and foreign nationals are all permitted to apply for the Instant Loan.\\n  * Every submission will be subject to Horizon Bank’s credit‑worthiness assessment.\\n\\nYou may request a credit facility provided you satisfy the following criteria:\\n- You are aged between {{faq_0ae0bb51_001}} and {{faq_0ae0bb51_002}} years.\\n- Your annual income is at least {{faq_0ae0bb51_003}} if you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\\n- Your annual income is at least {{faq_0ae0bb51_004}} if you are a foreigner holding a valid work pass.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_1946c44f\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps should I follow to request an Instant Loan from Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - Open the Horizon App, go to the **Money** menu, and select **Loan** to initiate the process.\\n- If you are not yet a Horizon customer, first download the Horizon App, then navigate to **Product Selection** and choose **Instant Loan** to begin your application.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_8984208c\", \"content\": \"Question: What charges does Horizon Bank apply to an Instant Loan?\\n\\nAnswer: - No annual fee is levied on Instant Loans that were originated before {{faq_8984208c_001}} February {{faq_8984208c_002}}.\\n- For Instant Loans opened on or after {{faq_8984208c_003}} February {{faq_8984208c_004}}:\\n  * A first‑year annual charge equal to {{faq_8984208c_005}} % of the loan amount is added to your Horizon credit card.\\n  * If the loan term is one year or longer, a {{faq_8984208c_006}} anniversary fee is assessed each year the loan remains outstanding, but only when the minimum payment on your Horizon credit card has not been received by its due date for the preceding {{faq_8984208c_007}} consecutive calendar months.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_952e4559\", \"content\": \"Question: What does Horizon Bank’s Instant Loan product involve?\\n\\nAnswer: Instant Loan is a Horizon Bank offering in Singapore that enables you to convert a portion of the available credit on your Horizon credit card into cash.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents. `customer_component` may already be elaborated with\n          retrieval-oriented wording the customer never actually said, so\n          if you set `unresolved_term` below, derive it by reasoning\n          directly against Original User Message and Trusted Conversation\n          Context instead -- never by quoting `customer_component` back --\n          a clarifying question must quote something the customer will\n          recognize as their own.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - The reverse matters just as much: a parent whose own subject is a\n          distinctly-named, different product or service is not material\n          merely because it is credit/loan-adjacent, belongs to the same\n          broader family, or is reached through the same in-app menu path as\n          the customer's named product. For example, a balance transfer\n          draws on loan credit and is filed under the app's \"Loan\" section\n          alongside a personal loan application -- but a parent describing\n          how to request a balance transfer does not materially answer a\n          request about applying for a (personal/general) loan. Do not let\n          shared category vocabulary or menu wording (\"Loan section\",\n          \"commence your application\") substitute for the parent actually\n          being about the specific product or process the customer named.\n          Only treat a differently-named product's parent as material when\n          it explicitly states it also applies to, or is the general form\n          of, the customer's named product.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a