{"timestamp": "2026-08-29T16:32:28.354+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_3e2f4119-8afe-4348-b435-558a24387f34", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n    PRE-DECOMPOSED CUSTOMER COMPONENTS (from Triage; already screened for financial relevance and compliance): [{'component_id': 'subquery_1', 'customer_component': 'What documents are required to apply for a Horizon Bank instant loan?'}, {'component_id': 'subquery_2', 'customer_component': 'Can I buy stocks through Horizon Bank?'}]\n    Each has `customer_component`, the retrieval-ready, context-resolved\n    wording -- use this for SEARCH tasks. For a CLARIFY component, do not\n    quote `customer_component` back to the customer (it may already be\n    elaborated with retrieval-oriented wording they never actually said) --\n    author `clarification.unresolved_request` by reasoning directly against\n    Latest User Input and Recent Conversation instead (see Rule 6 below).\n    This list is the complete, final partition of the customer's request. Do NOT merge, split, drop, or invent components — process every one exactly as given.\n\n    PRODUCT/INTENT MATRIX (Valid Nouns and Verbs):\n    {'ALL': ['Account Management', 'Authentication And Security', 'Features And Limits', 'General Inquiries', 'Payments And Transfers', 'Rewards And Promotions'], 'Credit_Card': ['Account Management', 'Application', 'Authentication And Security', 'Card Logistics', 'Eligibility', 'Features And Limits', 'Fees And Charges', 'General Inquiries', 'Interest And Rates', 'Loan And Credit Management', 'Payments And Transfers', 'Profile Updates', 'Rewards And Promotions', 'Transaction Disputes'], 'Debit_Card': ['Account Management', 'Application', 'Authentication And Security', 'Card Logistics', 'Eligibility', 'Features And Limits', 'Fees And Charges', 'General Inquiries', 'Payments And Transfers', 'Profile Updates', 'Rewards And Promotions', 'Transaction Disputes'], 'Deposit_Account': ['Account Management', 'Application', 'Authentication And Security', 'Branch And ATM Locator', 'Card Logistics', 'Eligibility', 'Features And Limits', 'Fees And Charges', 'General Inquiries', 'Interest And Rates', 'Payments And Transfers', 'Profile Updates', 'Rewards And Promotions', 'Transaction Disputes'], 'Horizon_APP': ['Account Management', 'Authentication And Security', 'Features And Limits', 'General Inquiries', 'Payments And Transfers', 'Profile Updates', 'Rewards And Promotions'], 'Insurance': ['Features And Limits', 'General Inquiries', 'Rewards And Promotions', 'Wealth And Insurance'], 'Mutual_Funds': ['Fees And Charges', 'General Inquiries', 'Wealth And Insurance'], 'Personal_Loan': ['Account Management', 'Application', 'Authentication And Security', 'Eligibility', 'Features And Limits', 'Fees And Charges', 'General Inquiries', 'Interest And Rates', 'Loan And Credit Management', 'Rewards And Promotions'], 'Rewards_Program': ['Authentication And Security', 'Features And Limits', 'General Inquiries', 'Payments And Transfers', 'Rewards And Promotions'], 'Stocks': ['Fees And Charges', 'General Inquiries', 'Wealth And Insurance']}\n\n    INTENT DEFINITION GUIDELINE:\n    \n1. Acquisition & Setup (Getting Started)\nApplication: How to apply, steps involved, document submission, or checking status. \nEligibility: Qualify for a product, income/age requirements, existing relationships. \nCard Logistics: Physical handling. Activation, delivery, reporting lost/stolen, replacement. \n2. Product Knowledge (Understanding the Asset)\nFeatures And Limits: General mechanics, benefits, usage limits, overseas use, digital wallets. \nFees And Charges: Costs, annual fees, fall-below fees, penalties, fee waivers. \nInterest And Rates: Interest accumulation, base rates, bonus criteria, payout timing. \n3. Daily Servicing (Account & Money Movement)\nAccount Management: Checking balances, dormancy, linking accounts, account cancellation. \nProfile Updates: Address, phone number, and email updates. \nPayments And Transfers: PayNow, FAST, GIRO, bill payments, cheque deposits, transfer errors. \nTransaction Disputes: Unrecognized charges, double billing, refunds, declined transactions. \n4. Specialized Financial Services\nLoan And Credit Management: Repayment schedules, installments, balance transfers, hardship. \nWealth And Insurance: Investments, stocks, mutual funds, auto-invest, insurance premiums, claims. \nRewards And Promotions: Earning points, cashback, merchant coupons, referral bonuses. \n5. Technical & General Support\nAuthentication And Security: Login issues, password/PIN resets, OTP failures, tokens, fraud. \nBranch And ATM Locator: Finding physical infrastructure. \nGeneral Inquiries: Catch-all. App navigation, UI bugs, compliance, generic notifications.\n\n\n    Active Context Matrix: [{'product': 'Deposit_Account', 'intents': ['Application']}, {'product': 'Credit_Card', 'intents': ['Application']}, {'product': 'Personal_Loan', 'intents': ['Account Management', 'Application', 'Authentication And Security', 'Eligibility', 'Features And Limits', 'Fees And Charges', 'General Inquiries', 'Interest And Rates', 'Loan And Credit Management', 'Rewards And Promotions']}]\n    Current Graph Context: active_plan=False, retrieved_knowledge=False\n    Recalled Prior-Session Context Is Available: False\n    Recent Conversation: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nUser: what else\nAI: I am here to help you with your Horizon Bank questions. 😊\nUser: what else\nAI: I am always here to assist you with your Horizon Bank questions. 😊\nUser: i want that\nAI: Could you please let me know a bit more about what you are looking for, such as whether you would like to learn more about the general services Horizon Bank offers or if you are interested in opening a new savings account? 🤔\nUser: the other one\nAI: Could you please clarify if you would like to learn more about the general services Horizon Bank offers or if you are interested in opening a new savings account? 🤔\nUser: I would like to learn more about the general services Horizon Bank offers.\nAI: I do not currently have information available regarding the general banking services offered by Horizon Bank. 🏦\nUser: how to open an account and how to apply credit card and can i also apply for loan if i have credit card\nAI: To open a savings account with Horizon Bank, you will need a mobile phone along with MyInfo verification to auto-populate your application form. If you delete or reinstall the Horizon App after successfully registering, you will still need to authenticate via SingPass when you log in again.\n\nTo apply for a credit card, Singaporean citizens and permanent residents can use MyInfo for expedited form completion on the secure Horizon Bank web portal, which can be initiated through a partner's mobile app or website. Foreign applicants should ensure they have their passport and most recent payslip ready for upload or photo capture via the Horizon App, in addition to accessing MyInfo. You will receive immediate status updates and prompts for any additional actions required within the app.\n\nIf you already possess a Horizon credit card and have an adequate unused credit limit, you may apply for Horizon Bank's Instant Loan offering, provided you meet the general eligibility criteria such as age limits and annual income requirements. Every submission is subject to Horizon Bank's credit-worthiness assessment.\nUser: what docs\nAI: To open a savings account with Horizon Bank, you will need a mobile phone along with MyInfo verification to auto-populate your application form. If you delete or reinstall the Horizon App after successfully registering, you will still need to authenticate via SingPass when you log in again.\n\nTo apply for a credit card, Singaporean citizens and permanent residents can use MyInfo for expedited form completion. Foreign applicants should ensure they have their passport and most recent payslip ready for upload or photo capture via the Horizon App, in addition to accessing MyInfo.\n\nI don't have information available regarding what documents are required to apply for a Horizon Bank instant loan.\nUser: no, i mean that, also can i buy stock?\n    User Baseline (advisory only; do not treat it as a current request): None\n    Latest User Input (context only; the components above are authoritative): \"no, i mean that, also can i buy stock?\"\n    TASK: Act as a Decoupled Database Search Architect.\n\n    CRITICAL RULES FOR ANGLE QUERIES:\n    - NEVER use conversational filler (e.g., \"Provide a guide\", \"Explain how to\", \"What is\").\n    - NEVER paraphrase the customer's original question in an angle.\n    - Each angle must be a short natural-language PHRASE (8-20 words) that reads like a sentence fragment from an FAQ answer.\n    - Use common banking vocabulary only. Do not invent specific product names, amounts, dates, or branch details.\n\n    1. CONTEXTUAL INHERITANCE: Read each component's customer_component text first. A Product or Intent may be inherited only when it is unambiguously established by the current-session trusted history, Active Context Matrix, or an active graph plan. Do not use the user baseline or prior-session recall to fill a missing Product or Intent, unless the component explicitly continues that recalled topic (for example, \"yes, continue\").\n    2. FOR EACH supplied component, evaluate the two mandatory retrieval foundations:\n       - PRODUCT: Identify the component's BASE product family by stripping any\n         descriptive qualifier, tier name, customer-segment word, or marketing\n         brand from the wording (e.g., \"business credit card\" -> base family\n         \"credit card\"; \"Flexible Loan\"/\"Instant Loan\" -> base family \"loan\";\n         \"joint savings account\" -> base family \"savings account\"). Match that\n         base family, not the qualified name, to the closest Matrix noun.\n         - If the qualifier names a product tier, plan, or marketing brand\n           (e.g., \"Flexible Loan\", \"Gold Card\", \"joint savings account\") --\n           anything other than a non-individual customer segment -- use the\n           matched base Matrix noun as PRODUCT; a qualifier is never grounds\n           to withhold PRODUCT here. Preserve the qualifier and every other\n           original word in this component's own customer_component output\n           field unchanged; base-product matching affects only PRODUCT/\n           target_commercial_product, never the wording shown to the customer\n           or judged by the evidence audit downstream. Whether that specific\n           qualified variant is actually covered is decided later, against\n           real retrieved evidence -- not here.\n         - If the qualifier instead names a non-individual customer segment\n           (business, corporate, institutional) rather than an individual\n           retail customer, do not set PRODUCT for SEARCH purposes at all --\n           this resolves as DECLINE (case b in Rule 3), since this\n           assistant's information is scoped exclusively to individual\n           banking regardless of whether the underlying base product exists.\n       - INTENT: a specific request type that maps to an intent in the PRODUCT/INTENT MATRIX.\n         A clearly-named product with NO discernible request type is exactly\n         as ambiguous as a request type with no product -- do not treat\n         PRODUCT as the only axis worth scrutinizing. If the component names\n         a product but gives no verb, action, or outcome at all (e.g. \"I\n         have a question about my loan\", \"something about my credit card\"),\n         or gives one so generic it could map to several genuinely different\n         intents for that same product with no basis to prefer one (e.g.\n         \"help