{"timestamp": "2026-08-30T06:25:39.205+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_verify_nextactions3_1788071131", "user_id": "verify_nextactions3", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): tell me about the Horizon Rewards credit card\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nUser: tell me about the Horizon Rewards credit card\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Access card details through the mobile app or by logging into your online banking portal.\", \"policy\": \"Review the terms and conditions regarding card usage limits and reward point expiration policies.\", \"conceptual\": \"The credit card offers various benefits including reward points on eligible transactions and digital wallet integration.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Credit_Card\", \"target_intent\": [\"Features And Limits\", \"Rewards And Promotions\"], \"customer_component\": \"Provide information about the features and details of the Horizon Rewards credit card.\", \"direct_query\": \"Provide information about the features and details of the Horizon Rewards credit card.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Access card details through the mobile app or by logging into your online banking portal.\", \"policy\": \"Review the terms and conditions regarding card usage limits and reward point expiration policies.\", \"conceptual\": \"The credit card offers various benefits including reward points on eligible transactions and digital wallet integration.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_c85dae7e\", \"content\": \"Question: What benefits and capabilities come with the Horizon Link credit card?\\n\\nAnswer: - **Reward programme**: Earn the highest points on FairPrice Group grocery and food purchases. See the Horizon App for details on union and non‑union member tiers – subject to standard terms and conditions.\\n- **Zero‑fee structure**: No annual fee, no foreign‑currency surcharge and no over‑limit penalties.\\n- **Customisable repayment**: Select a due‑date that works for you and settle the balance at your convenience.\\n- **Enhanced online security**: {{faq_c85dae7e_001}}D Secure verification is built into the Horizon App for safer e‑commerce transactions.\\n- **Personal security controls**: Instantly lock or unlock your card and adjust payment preferences directly from the app.\\n- **Card pairing**: Seamlessly link your Horizon Link credit card with your Horizon debit card to switch between credit and savings accounts as needed.\\n- **Instant digital card issuance**: Receive a virtual card in the Horizon App immediately, ready for online and contactless purchases via Apple Pay or Google Pay.\\n- **NFC‑enabled physical activation**: Tap the back of your phone to the card for one‑click activation – a first in Singapore.\\n- **Real‑time rewards tracking**: Monitor your Linkpoints as you spend, with instant updates in the app.\\n- **Spending insights**: View categorized expenses and an overall spending summary in one dashboard.\\n- **Spend monitoring tool**: Keep tabs on your purchasing habits through the built‑in tracker.\\n- **Secure PIN setup**: Choose a six‑digit PIN within the Horizon App to protect ATM withdrawals.\\n- **Numberless card feature**: The card number is hidden and can be accessed securely via the app, reducing fraud risk.\\n- **Eco‑friendly design**: Card is manufactured from recycled ocean plastic, and the welcome pack uses recycled paper to minimise environmental impact.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_ff64508d\", \"content\": \"Question: What rewards do the Horizon Link Credit Card and Horizon Link Debit Card provide, and how can I earn them?\\n\\nAnswer: - **FPG spend definition**: Purchases made at FairPrice, FairPrice Finest, FairPrice Xtra, FairPrice Xpress, FairPrice Online, Warehouse Club, Unity and Cheers (excluding Cheers and FairPrice Xpress outlets inside Esso stations) as well as qualifying Kopitiam food stalls are classified as FPG spend. The transaction must be posted before it can count toward rewards.\\n- **Eligible spend**: \\n  • *Local eligible spend* – All Visa transactions in Singapore dollars processed in Singapore, except FPG spend and any excluded categories. You earn {{faq_ff64508d_001}} % Linkpoints on this spend, with no upper limit. For supplementary cards, points are credited to the primary account holder.\\n  • *Foreign eligible spend* – All Visa transactions not in Singapore dollars or processed outside Singapore (including DCC conversions), again excluding FPG spend and prohibited transactions. The same {{faq_ff64508d_002}} % Linkpoints rate applies, uncapped, and points for supplementary cards go to the main holder.\\n- **Minimum monthly spend**: The sum of local and foreign eligible spend must meet a monthly threshold to unlock bonus rates. This requirement is waived for the calendar month in which your card is first approved.\\n- **Base rate**: FPG grocery purchases earn a {{faq_ff64508d_003}} % Linkpoints rebate automatically. FairPrice members (NTUC Union shareholders) receive an additional {{faq_ff64508d_004}} % rebate on FPG groceries (excluding Cheers), capped at {{faq_ff64508d_005}} Linkpoints per year.\\n- **Monthly bonus**: Once the minimum monthly spend is satisfied, you receive a {{faq_ff64508d_006}} % Linkpoints rebate on all FPG spend with the credit card, or a {{faq_ff64508d_007}} % rebate on the Horizon Link Debit Card. A monthly Linkpoints cap limits the total points you can earn from FPG spend in any given month.\\n- **Quarterly bonus**: After meeting the minimum spend for three consecutive months, you qualify for a {{faq_ff64508d_008}} % Linkpoints rebate on FPG spend ({{faq_ff64508d_009}} % on the debit card) with a cap of {{faq_ff64508d_010}} Linkpoints ({{faq_ff64508d_011}} for the debit card). An additional tier provides a {{faq_ff64508d_012}} % rebate ({{faq_ff64508d_013}} % on the debit card) once the higher spend threshold ({{faq_ff64508d_014}} for credit, {{faq_ff64508d_015}} for debit) is met for three straight months, also capped at {{faq_ff64508d_016}} ({{faq_ff64508d_017}}) Linkpoints.\\n- **FairPrice member extra bonus**: FairPrice members enjoy an extra {{faq_ff64508d_018}} % bonus on FPG grocery purchases (excluding Cheers), subject to AGM approval and limited to {{faq_ff64508d_019}} Linkpoints annually.\\n- **Non‑union cardholders**: The same eligibility rules apply, but the base rebate is limited to {{faq_ff64508d_020}} % on FPG groceries, and the quarterly bonus rates are {{faq_ff64508d_021}} % (or {{faq_ff64508d_022}} % on the debit card) with a {{faq_ff64508d_023}}‑point cap, plus an extra {{faq_ff64508d_024}} % (or {{faq_ff64508d_025}} % on the debit card) for higher spend levels, both subject to the same three‑month consecutive spend condition.\\n\\nFor a complete list of excluded transactions and detailed product terms, please refer to the Horizon Bank FAQs and the Horizon Link Card Terms & Conditions.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_a6245ed5\", \"content\": \"Question: How do I benefit from the Horizon Bank's seasonal credit card promotion, and what rewards can I expect between March and July?\\n\\nAnswer: As part of our Credit Card Acquisition Giveaway, you'll be eligible for a special incentive. Upon fulfilling the promotional requirements within the specified timeframe, you can look forward to receiving a digital scratch card, conveniently accessible through the Horizon App, under the 'Rewards' section, specifically within the 'Quests' tab.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents. `customer_component` may already be elaborated with\n          retrieval-oriented wording the customer never actually said, so\n          if you set `unresolved_term` below, derive it by reasoning\n          directly against Original User Message and Trusted Conversation\n          Context instead -- never by quoting `customer_component` back --\n          a clarifying question must quote something the customer will\n          recognize as their own.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - The reverse matters just as much: a parent whose own subject is a\n          distinctly-named, different product or service is not material\n          merely because it is credit/loan-adjacent, belongs to the same\n          broader family, or is reached through the same in-app menu path as\n          the customer's named product. For example, a balance transfer\n          draws on loan credit and is filed under the app's \"Loan\" section\n          alongside a personal loan application -- but a parent describing\n          how to request a balance transfer does not materially answer a\n          request about applying for a (personal/general) loan. Do not let\n          shared category vocabulary or menu wording (\"Loan section\",\n          \"commence your application\") substitute for the parent actually\n          being about the specific product or process the customer named.\n          Only treat a differently-named product's parent as material when\n          it explicitly states it also applies to, or is the general form\n          of, the customer's named product.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n        - PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT: selected parents provide grounded, material\n          information for one meaningful part of the `customer_component`,\n          while another material part has no useful related evidence. Select\n          only the supporting parent IDs; the backend will retain them while\n          retrieval continues.\n        - INSUFFICIENT: the supplied parents provide no grounded, materially\n          relevant inf