arly if you are applying for a Horizon credit card.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_46c43248\", \"content\": \"Question: Can I open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - You are eligible to apply for a Horizon Bank Savings Account if you meet both of the following criteria:\\n  {{faq_46c43248_001}}. You are a Singapore citizen, a Singapore permanent resident, or a foreign national holding a valid work pass.\\n  {{faq_46c43248_002}}. You are {{faq_46c43248_003}} years of age or older.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_098d72b7\", \"content\": \"Question: Is it possible to open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - You may apply for a Horizon Bank Savings Account if you satisfy both of the following conditions:\\n  {{faq_098d72b7_001}}. You are a Singapore citizen, a Singapore permanent resident, or a foreign national holding a valid work pass;\\n  {{faq_098d72b7_002}}. You are at least {{faq_098d72b7_003}} years old.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_cc2bb0f9\", \"content\": \"Question: What prerequisites must I meet to open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - A mobile device and MyInfo authentication are sufficient to auto‑populate your application form.\\n- If you delete or reinstall the Horizon App after completing registration, you will still need to use SingPass to verify your identity when you log in again.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_70aebcd6\", \"content\": \"Question: What information and tools are necessary to open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - A mobile phone together with MyInfo verification to auto‑populate your application form.\\n- If you delete or reinstall the Horizon App after successfully registering, you will still need to authenticate via SingPass when you log in again.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_1b9ab045\", \"content\": \"Question: Why did Horizon Bank reject my credit card application?\\n\\nAnswer: - Every credit card request undergoes an internal review, and we evaluate each submission thoroughly. Typical reasons for a denial include:\\n- Insufficient earnings:\\n  • Singapore citizen or Permanent Resident aged {{faq_1b9ab045_001}}‑{{faq_1b9ab045_002}} with yearly income under {{faq_1b9ab045_003}}\\n  • Singapore citizen or Permanent Resident aged {{faq_1b9ab045_004}}+ with yearly income under {{faq_1b9ab045_005}}\\n  • Non‑resident ({{faq_1b9ab045_006}} years or older) earning less than {{faq_1b9ab045_007}} annually\\n- Having already reached the maximum credit exposure allowed across all banks\\n- Existing overdue obligations with other financial institutions\\n- Absence of a recent Notice of Assessment or CPF contribution record\\n- Applicant is younger than {{faq_1b9ab045_008}} years old\\n\\nIf you were declined, you may still consider opening a Horizon savings account, which offers up to {{faq_1b9ab045_009}} p.a. on the first {{faq_1b9ab045_010}} deposited and can provide up to an {{faq_1b9ab045_011}} return when paired with a Horizon debit card (subject to terms and conditions). To start the savings account application, simply:\\n- Uninstall the Horizon App\\n- Re‑install the Horizon App from the app store\\n- Submit a savings‑account request through the app\\n\\nPlease note that Singapore‑dollar deposits held by non‑bank depositors are protected by the Singapore Deposit Insurance Corporation up to {{faq_1b9ab045_012}} per depositor across all Scheme members, as mandated by law.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_586ee40c\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the typical time required to complete a Horizon Bank application?\\n\\nAnswer: - The submission usually takes only a few minutes.\\n- If further clarification is needed and we must contact you, the process may extend to a maximum of five business days.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_357dd970\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the typical duration for completing a Horizon Bank application?\\n\\nAnswer: - The submission is usually processed within a few minutes.\\n- Should we need to reach out for further clarification,