{"timestamp": "2026-08-30T07:50:10.058+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_verify_feedback_scope_1788076198", "user_id": "verify_feedback", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): how to open my account\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nUser: how to open my account\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Complete the online application form, submit required identification documents, and verify your identity through the portal.\", \"policy\": \"Applicants must be at least eighteen years old and provide valid government-issued identification for account opening.\", \"conceptual\": \"A deposit account is a financial product held at a bank that provides security for your funds.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Deposit_Account\", \"target_intent\": [\"Account Management\", \"Application\", \"Authentication And Security\", \"Branch And ATM Locator\", \"Card Logistics\", \"Eligibility\", \"Features And Limits\", \"Fees And Charges\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Interest And Rates\", \"Payments And Transfers\", \"Profile Updates\", \"Rewards And Promotions\", \"Transaction Disputes\"], \"customer_component\": \"How to open a bank account with Horizon Bank.\", \"direct_query\": \"How to open a bank account with Horizon Bank.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Complete the online application form, submit required identification documents, and verify your identity through the portal.\", \"policy\": \"Applicants must be at least eighteen years old and provide valid government-issued identification for account opening.\", \"conceptual\": \"A deposit account is a financial product held at a bank that provides security for your funds.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [\"faq_70aebcd6\", \"faq_1b9ab045\", \"faq_586ee40c\", \"faq_357dd970\"], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"faq_70aebcd6\", \"faq_1b9ab045\", \"faq_586ee40c\", \"faq_357dd970\"], \"reason\": \"The provided parents contain information on the application process for specific account types (Savings Account) and general application timelines, but do not provide a comprehensive guide for opening a general 'bank account' as requested by the user.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_70aebcd6\", \"fact\": \"Opening a Savings Account requires a mobile phone and MyInfo verification.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_1b9ab045\", \"fact\": \"Savings account applications are submitted through the Horizon App.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_586ee40c\", \"fact\": \"Application submissions are typically processed within a few minutes, with a maximum of five business days if clarification is required.\"}]}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_10f9fec0\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the requirements to open a new Horizon Bank account?\\n\\nAnswer: To initiate the application process for a Horizon Bank account, simply utilize your mobile device and authenticate through MyInfo, which will expedite the pre-filling of your application in a secure manner. For non-Singaporean residents, please be prepared to upload a valid passport and relevant income documentation, particularly if you are applying for a Horizon credit card.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_46c43248\", \"content\": \"Question: Can I open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - You are eligible to apply for a Horizon Bank Savings Account if you meet both of the following criteria:\\n  {{faq_46c43248_001}}. You are a Singapore citizen, a Singapore permanent resident, or a foreign national holding a valid work pass.\\n  {{faq_46c43248_002}}. You are {{faq_46c43248_003}} years of age or older.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_098d72b7\", \"content\": \"Question: Is it possible to open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - You may apply for a Horizon Bank Savings Account if you satisfy both of the following conditions:\\n  {{faq_098d72b7_001}}. You are a Singapore citizen, a Singapore permanent resident, or a foreign national holding a valid work pass;\\n  {{faq_098d72b7_002}}. You are at least {{faq_098d72b7_003}} years old.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_cc2bb0f9\", \"content\": \"Question: What prerequisites must I meet to open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - A mobile device and MyInfo authentication are sufficient to auto‑populate your application form.\\n- If you delete or reinstall the Horizon App after completing registration, you will still need to use SingPass to verify your identity when you log in again.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_70aebcd6\", \"content\": \"Question: What information and tools are necessary to open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - A mobile phone together with MyInfo verification to auto‑populate your application form.\\n- If you delete or reinstall the Horizon App after successfully registering, you will still need to authenticate via SingPass when you log in again.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_1b9ab045\", \"content\": \"Question: Why did Horizon Bank reject my credit card application?\\n\\nAnswer: - Every credit card request undergoes an internal review, and we evaluate each submission thoroughly. Typical reasons for a denial include:\\n- Insufficient earnings:\\n  • Singapore citizen or Permanent Resident aged {{faq_1b9ab045_001}}‑{{faq_1b9ab045_002}} with yearly income under {{faq_1b9ab045_003}}\\n  • Singapore citizen or Permanent Resident aged {{faq_1b9ab045_004}}+ with yearly income under {{faq_1b9ab045_005}}\\n  • Non‑resident ({{faq_1b9ab045_006}} years or older) earning less than {{faq_1b9ab045_007}} annually\\n- Having already reached the maximum credit exposure allowed across all banks\\n- Existing overdue obligations with other financial institutions\\n- Absence of a recent Notice of Assessment or CPF contribution record\\n- Applicant is younger than {{faq_1b9ab045_008}} years old\\n\\nIf you were declined, you may still consider opening a Horizon savings account, which offers up to {{faq_1b9ab045_009}} p.a. on the first {{faq_1b9ab045_010}} deposited and can provide up to an {{faq_1b9ab045_011}} return when paired with a Horizon debit card (subject to terms and conditions). To start the savings account application, simply:\\n- Uninstall the Horizon App\\n- Re‑install the Horizon App from the app store\\n- Submit a savings‑account request through the app\\n\\nPlease note that Singapore‑dollar deposits held by non‑bank depositors are protected by the Singapore Deposit Insurance Corporation up to {{faq_1b9ab045_012}} per depositor across all Scheme members, as mandated by law.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_586ee40c\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the typical time required to complete a Horizon Bank application?\\n\\nAnswer: - The submission usually takes only a few minutes.\\n- If further clarification is needed and we must contact you, the process may extend to a maximum of five business days.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_357dd970\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the typical duration for completing a Horizon Bank application?\\n\\nAnswer: - The submission is usually processed within a few minutes.\\n- Should we need to reach out for further clarification, the review period can extend to as long as five business days.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents. `customer_component` may already be elaborated with\n          retrieval-oriented wording the customer never actually said, so\n          if you set `unresolved_term` below, derive it by reasoning\n          directly against Original User Message and Trusted Conversation\n          Context instead -- never by quoting `customer_component` back --\n          a clarifying question must quote something the customer will\n          recognize as their own.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - The reverse matters just as much: a parent whose own subject is a\n          distinctly-named, different product or service is not material\n          merely because it is credit/loan-adjacent, belongs to the same\n          broader family, or is reached through the same in-app menu path as\n          the customer's named product. For example, a balance transfer\n          draws on loan credit and is filed under the app's \"Loan\" section\n          alongside a personal loan application -- but a parent describing\n          how to request a balance transfer does not materially answer a\n          request about applying for a (personal/general) loan. Do not let\n          shared category vocabulary or menu wording (\"Loan section\",\n          \"commence your application\") substitute for the parent actually\n          being about the specific product or process the customer named.\n          Only treat a differently-named product's parent as material when\n          it explicitly states it also applies to, or is the general form\n          of, the customer's named product.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n        - PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT: selected parents provide grounded, material\n          information for one meaningful part of the `customer_component`,\n          while another material part has no useful related evidence. Select\n          only the supporting parent IDs; the backend will retain them while\n          retrieval continues.\n        - INSUFFICIENT: the supplied parents provide no grounded, materially\n          relevant information that could be usefully presented in response to\n          the `customer_component`.\n        - For INSUFFICIENT, also set `likely_ambiguous_request`: true only\n          when the retrieval genuinely failed because `customer_component`\n          itself is under-specified or could